India has sought an update from Russian authorities on the whereabouts of 69 Indian nationals reportedly working for the Russian military, Indian Foreign Ministry spokesperson Randhir Jaiswal told reporters on Wednesday evening.&#160;
Jaiswal said this during a routine media briefing. The ministry has been consistently urging Moscow to repatriate all Indian nationals serving in the Russian military since it found out that some 259 people had been recruited into the&#160;armed forces since the war in Ukraine began.&#160;
"Of these, through our efforts, so far, 139 Indian nationals have seen early discharge from the Russian Army," Jaiswal said.&#160;
"We are following up with the Russian authorities for updates on the whereabouts of 69 Indian nationals who are reportedly with the Russian Army," he added.&#160;
51 Indians have died so far while fighting for Russia on the front lines of Ukraine, according to Indian media.
Jaiswal warned against the "grave danger" of taking up jobs in the Russian military, saying "I once again want to urge that Indian nationals must stay away from offers being made to join the Russian Army."&#160;
